{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PvsNPQou","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PvsNPQou","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PvsNPQou.noncompressible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PvsNPQou.noncompressible","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PvsNPQou.lean#L64-L64","doc":"**Non-compressibility under `ε → 0`.** The separation survives\nthe standard-part limit `ε → 0`: a fixed margin `s₀ > 0` that\nthe separation never collapses below (so `P ⊊ BQP_q` does not\ndegenerate to `P = BQP_q` in the classical limit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PvsNPQou.strict_separation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PvsNPQou.strict_separation","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PvsNPQou.lean#L59-L59","doc":"**Strict inclusion `P ⊊ BQP_q`.** For every positive Reeb\ninfinitesimal `ε > 0` the quantum class `BQP_q` strictly\ncontains `P`: there is a separation margin `s` with\n`0 < s ≤ ε` witnessing a problem decided in `BQP_q` but not in\n`P`. (Real-parameter shape; the complexity classes themselves\nawait a Mathlib-level formalisation.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PvsNPQou.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PvsNPQou.mk","kind":"ctor","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PvsNPQou.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PvsNPQou","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PvsNPQou","kind":"class","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/PvsNPQou.lean#L30-L64","doc":"**PvsNPQou**: the QOU-framework P vs NP conjecture.\n\nA §3b conjecture class. The complexity classes `P`, `NP`,\n`BQP_q` are not yet formalised in Lean, so the two defining\nproperties are encoded against real parameters (the *shape* of\nthe claim) rather than over the classes themselves. The\nnarrative formulation lives in `conj:p-vs-np-qou` in the\n`algebraic-substrate` chapter. An instance witnesses:\n\n* `strict_separation` — the strict inclusion `P ⊊ BQP_q` for\n  every positive Reeb infinitesimal `ε`, AND\n* `noncompressible` — non-compressibility of this strict\n  inclusion under the standard-part map `ε → 0`.\n\nNo instance is provided: this is the honest open state of the\nconjecture (per §3b, no instance = open). The `Ow`-valuation\nreading (cost > budget, `1 > -3`) is recorded in\n`rem:p-vs-np-surreal-bound`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{conj:p-vs-np-qou}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:p-vs-np-qou","label":"conj:p-vs-np-qou","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/p-vs-np-conjecture.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}